Agentic commerce refers to the use of AI agents to autonomously discover, evaluate, and complete transactions on behalf of buyers within digital interfaces:

| For businesses | To get started with agentic commerce, use Enable in-context selling on AI agents, built on the Agentic Commerce Protocol. |
| --- | --- |
| For marketplaces | If you’re a platform or marketplace and want to offer in-context selling on AI agents, see our guide for platforms and marketplaces. |

If you operate an AI platform, use agentic commerce to let buyers transact directly with businesses in your app. Use the SharedPaymentToken object to pass payment credentials and risk signals to businesses without exposing underlying credentials. Shared payment tokens (SPTs) are scoped and time-constrained to a single transaction for added security.
